WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.370
Green means it keeps going up next, right?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.805
One candle records four prices for one period: open, high, low and close.

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:18.860
This is made-up five-minute data. It's not a promise about the next five minutes.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.631
The body shows the gap between open and close.

00:00:34.631 --> 00:00:37.736
The wicks mark the highest and lowest prices in that period.

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:41.100
A candle that hasn't finished yet keeps changing with new trades.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.450
Why does the chart look different when I switch the time frame?

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.462
Each candle now covers a different length of time.

00:01:06.462 --> 00:01:10.800
Read the time frame first, then the shape. Don't mistake five minutes for a day.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.901
Apps may use different colours for up and down, so read the legend and the numbers.

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:33.160
Past moves can be informative, but one candle can't guarantee the next move.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.610
High 51,000. Close 50,500.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:52.260
Read the record first. Don't treat a record as a prophecy.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.850
'I have 1,000 and only want to risk 20. So I go all in? ' Next: how much to buy.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.440
Understand first, then act.
